  "notes": [
    "REMOVED from prior version: W&M Fire Protection (Plantsville) - acquired Dec 2007 by Davis-Ulmer, well before the 2015 cutoff, and corporate HQ is now Hawthorne NY; Plantsville is a branch.",
    "REMOVED from candidate list: Legacy Fire Protection (Impact Fire, 2021) - HQ is Ludlow MA, not CT.",
    "EXCLUDED, corporate carve-out: Stanley Access Technologies, Farmington - $900M automatic-entrance division sold by Stanley Black & Decker to Allegion, closed Jul 2022. Real and large, but a division sale, not an independent going away. Add on request.",
    "EXCLUDED, manufacturer: ComNet (Communications Networks), Danbury - video transmission hardware maker, acquired by ACRE Dec 2016. Not a service company.",
    "EXCLUDED, distributors: Orchard Lock Distributors (Hamden) to Lockmasters, Jan 2025; OKEE Industries (West Hartford) to Cook & Boardman, Jun 2024. Both wholesale suppliers, consistent with the roster's exclusion of distributors. Would make a good sub-section if wanted.",
    "Pye-Barker's Brookfield location page reads 'formerly United Alarm | Homeguard' - the two deals appear to have been consolidated into one branch.",
    "Hartford Sprinkler is HQ'd in Bloomfield despite the name. P&J Sprinkler city resolved from UNK to Willimantic.",
    "Four deals could not be dated from any source: Integrated Protection Services, United Alarm, Allstate Fire Equipment, ProTechs. They print without a year rather than with a guess."
  ]
